A person borrows ₹8,000 at a simple interest rate of 7.5% per annum. How much interest will he pay after 2 years?

A) ₹1,000
B) ₹1,100
C) ₹1,200
D) ₹1,500

Answer: C) ₹1,200

Explanation:

Simple Interest:

$$ SI=\frac{P\times R\times T}{100} $$

Here:

p=8000
R=7.5%
T=2years
SI=\frac{8000\times7.5\times2}{100} =₹1200 

Therefore:

₹1,200
	​
